oster seed 1, against main 4b1bded; three seeds, runs diverge, so only large or all-seed differences count). **It is nitrogen-limited and does not collapse.** Plants (kind 0) hold 2.4 x 10^8 / 7.6 x 10^8 / 3.4 x 10^8 kg (1.9%, 6.2%, 1.7% of the baseline's 1.28 / 1.24 / 2.02 x 10^10) in 1.6 x 10^8 / 4.3 x 10^8 / 1.8 x 10^9 members, matter 2.0 / 2.1 / 1.1% of their mass (4.7 / 5.1 / 5.7%), real life 0.28 / 0.66 / 0.36 y (0.36 / 0.39 / 0.61), adult life 0.33 / 0.65 / 0.36 (0.52 / 0.57 / 0.70), 6.0 x 10^8 / 6.3 x 10^8 / 4.7 x 10^9 births a year (1.1 x 10^11 / 3.9 x 10^10 / 3.5 x 10^10); **the births by month lose the spring peak** (months 5, 4 and 6 of 12, 13 to 14% of the year in a month, in the baseline; months 8 to 11, 11 to 12% in a month, in the nitrogen runs: flatter, in the autumn, as the nitrogen rot gives back comes with the warm months; month numbers from 1), and the share of building attempts the mineral held back (`nlim`) is 0.73 / 0.87 / 0.87. The members are small (a median member of 0.1 kg) and many nodes: 17,500 / 6,200 / 18,900 bodies at year 60 (2,500 / 2,900 / 4,100). Eaters (kind 1) hold 1.3 x 10^8 / 3.2 x 10^8 / 2.1 x 10^8 kg (25%, 33%, 16% of 5.2 x 10^8 / 9.5 x 10^8 / 1.3 x 10^9), 1.2 x 10^6 / 2.9 x 10^6 / 1.3 x 10^6 members (6.2 x 10^6 / 1.6 x 10^7 / 1.6 x 10^7), live 1.63 / 1.67 / 3.32 y really (1.36 / 0.83 / 1.35), adults 6.1 / 3.1 / 10.6 y (2.5 / 1.5 / 1.7), births 8.2 x 10^5 / 2.1 x 10^6 / 5.2 x 10^5 a year (5.3 x 10^6 / 2 x 10^7 / 1.4 x 10^7), still in the months 7 to 9 of 12, `nlim` 0.40 / 0.41 / 0.49: they are much less limited than the plants (they eat the dead matter, which holds the nitrogen). **Carbon gas** at year 60: 361 / 360 / 362 ppm (118 / 177 / 86 in the baseline): the dead matter that locked carbon (review 8) cannot be built, so the air keeps it. **Seconds a year** (3 runs at once on 4 cores, another job running): 6.7 / 1.6 / 5.8 (0.74 / 0.97 / 1.11): the many small nodes (26 / 21 / 33 us a body update against 17 / 17 / 20), not